  "facts": [
    "Built between 1978 and 1980, the Minillas Tunnel stretches 396 meters, or 1,299 feet, and carries six lanes—three in each direction—through San Juan’s bustling urban core.",
    "By 2012, the Minillas Tunnel handled an impressive 211,700 vehicles daily, making it one of Puerto Rico’s busiest and most critical traffic arteries.",
    "The tunnel’s name honors the historic Minillas neighborhood, and its construction marked a pivotal upgrade to Puerto Rico Highway 22, the unsigned Interstate PR‑2."
